    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6c737b17905b900b942fa540e998fcae514a3d5bd1d7a5ea8fe785fc22f6f2e9",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Across the time, quadratic-character, and cusp-form settings, the source expands a tunable resonator inside baseline and target-weighted averages, uses the setting's averaging law to reduce those averages to finite quadratic forms, and then compares the target-weighted form with resonator energy. Fourier decay leaves equality and mk=n incidences, discriminant averaging leaves odd-square products, and Petersson orthogonality, after Hecke multiplication, leaves a diagonal energy form and a gcd-sensitive target kernel.",
