    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_73e55a75653fba905f4e29b48a8369af3680a556942df18404fb6041813ff1d2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The usable resonator length is governed by the highest moment and the ambient orthogonality error that must be controlled. The zeta maximum uses the near-full N=T^(1-epsilon) diagonal quadratic ratio, the moderate-frequency regime can bypass a tuned resonator using the second and fourth zeta moments, and the rarer-value argument shortens to N<=T^(1/2-epsilon) so the resonator fourth moment is diagonal. Quadratic-character errors and the Petersson-Bessel range impose their own family-specific length restrictions.",
