    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8c99e59cdef44c278a3eca2d98522d18a757d196decdb641e8181d934e0948a6",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source repeatedly combines two steps: choose squarefree multiplicative coefficients on a tuned prime window so favorable cross terms become local Euler factors, then use a positive Rankin tilt to compare the finite resonator sums with their factorizable infinite extensions. This pairing supplies the zeta correlation gain, controls the zeta fourth-moment cost, and justifies the quadratic-family and cusp-form product evaluations at their chosen finite lengths.",
