      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_90d43e7fefc3daa904971dc60f76bb3dc820458d14d9fb549575a99934cf711d",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "In both the quadratic-character and cusp-form families, the untwisted coefficient choice f gives constructive prime-level correlation for a large-value witness, while replacing f by mu f reverses the linear prime contribution and supplies the small-value witness. The quadratic-family unit displays the negative local factor for mu f and states the f counterpart; the cusp-form unit displays the positive local factor for f and states the mu f counterpart.",
